ions is best supported by the sample data?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186213674 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "At least $88%$ of all consumers will dislike this ad." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186211882} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Exactly $88%$ of all consumers will dislike this ad." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186211883} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Most people who like this smartphone brand will dislike the ad." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186211884} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "At least $88%$ of all smartphone users will dislike this ad." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186211885} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Most people who dislike this smartphone brand will like the ad." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186211886}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186211881}] :question/math-academy-id "q-301319" :question/problem "A technology company randomly selected $300$ people from a list of customers who said they like the company’s flagship smartphone brand. The $300$ customers were shown a new advertisement for the brand and then asked whether they liked or disliked the ad. Of those surveyed, $88%$ said they disliked the ad. Which of the following inferences can appropriately be drawn from this survey result?"}] :knowledge-point/title "Further Generalizing Sample Results" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048706 :topic/math-academy-id 6215 :topic/title "Interpreting Survey Results"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186213099 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186213675 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186211888} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186211889} {:ans